awn at (Qufim Island (F-8)) during thunder weather.\010 Supports 3 parties. \010 Be careful with Gigas (Giants), they hit quite hard, especially Gigas Hunter (the RNG-type that throws rocks).\010 Blue Mage - Learnable - Grand Slam | Screwdriver\01023-27\010Meriphataud Mountains [Horizon change] \010 (Meriphataud Mountains (D-10)) \010 (Meriphataud Mountains (G-10))\010 Ridge Lizard [Horizon change] (29-31)\010 Puma [Horizon change] (29-33)\010 Drooling Hound [Horizon change] (31-35)\010 Not a a bad walk from Outpost or Crag of Mea.\010 Can be done at level 23 if going slow between pulls, at level 25, Drooling Hounds can enter rotation. EXP tapers during level 26 but can still produce 8-10k exp/hr without rings because kills go quickly. Easy chain 5's with a solid party. \010 Puma inflicts Paralysis (Blaster) and Silence (Chaotic Eye.) Chaotic Eye is a very quick cast, so be careful.\010",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Level 20-30\010\010 Lizard's Blockhead TP move can hit non-tanks for very high numbers (200+ dmg.) Be careful about pulling too much enmity!\010 Beware Drooling Hound (31-33) at night, it has AoE Disease.\010 Supports 2 parties, 1 at each coordinate.\010 Blue Mage - Learnable - Chaotic Eye | Poison Breath\01024-26\010Ranguemont Pass\010 (Ranguemont Pass (J-5))\010 (Ranguemont Pass (I-8))\010 Stirge (30-33)\010 Hecteyes (31-33)\010 ~12 minute walk from Ronfaure Outpost.\010 Sight and Sound aggro en route to camp.\010 (Ranguemont Pass (J-5)) has about 8 Stirge spawns along the tunnel. May need to roam a bit. \010 Blue Mage - Learnable - Death Ray | Blood Drain\01024-27\010Sauromugue Champaign\010 (Sauromugue Champaign (I-7))\010 Sauromugue Skink (28-32)\010 Diving Beetle (30-32)\010 Yagudo Interrogator\010 Yagudo Oracle\010 Yagudo Priest\010 Yagudo Theologist\010 Yagudo Votary (26-36)\010 Camp at fallen pillar/crumbling wall or outside of fort.\010 Mob density a bit scarce. Yagudo have a large level range.\01024-27\010Carpenters' Landing\